1
00:00:01,208 --> 00:00:02,792
The truth is...

2
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:09,208
I like guys.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,042
Tell me it's not true, Sui!

4
00:00:28,458 --> 00:00:29,833
Thanks for the food.

5
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:36,792
You're in a great mood today.

6
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:41,542
I know why.

7
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:44,125
Something happened
after Sports Day, didn't it?

8
00:00:45,292 --> 00:00:46,542
No.

9
00:00:48,625 --> 00:00:52,125
It's definitely about that senpai again.

10
00:00:56,625 --> 00:00:59,292
[Room 208: Kishida Sui, Kurobe Harutora]

11
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,958
Thank goodness, there you are.

12
00:01:15,792 --> 00:01:17,958
You haven't turned your
sign-out tag back in yet.

13
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:21,042
Oh, I forgot to put it back.

14
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,917
Sorry, I'm just a little...

15
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:30,917
I'm sorry.

16
00:01:41,292 --> 00:01:42,958
Did something happen?

17
00:01:43,083 --> 00:01:45,500
No, it's nothing.

18
00:01:47,118 --> 00:01:48,168
But you don't look okay at all...

19
00:01:48,193 --> 00:01:52,708
No, really, I'm just
exhausted from studying.

20
00:01:53,792 --> 00:01:54,792
Senpai!

21
00:02:02,292 --> 00:02:04,208
You wouldn't understand, Harutora.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,125
Huh?

23
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:02,667
"Hold on, Harutora-kun"
[Episode 8]

24
00:03:16,708 --> 00:03:18,250
What are you doing?

25
00:03:18,917 --> 00:03:21,250
The national tournament preliminaries
are tomorrow.

26
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:23,083
Let's head back inside.

27
00:03:32,708 --> 00:03:34,083
I see.

28
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:39,333
So Kishida senpai won't tell you anything.

29
00:03:42,167 --> 00:03:43,750
Yeah...

30
00:03:47,708 --> 00:03:50,250
All you can really do right now
is give him some space, right?

31
00:03:51,708 --> 00:03:52,917
Huh?

32
00:03:53,792 --> 00:03:58,625
What you can do right now
is win tomorrow's game.

33
00:04:01,083 --> 00:04:02,500
What else could you do?

34
00:04:06,417 --> 00:04:08,917
If you're off your game,

35
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:13,875
won't Kishida senpai feel even more guilty?

36
00:04:15,917 --> 00:04:17,083
That's true.

37
00:04:20,667 --> 00:04:21,667
You make a good point.

38
00:04:31,042 --> 00:04:34,375
What a waste! Are you gonna throw that out?

39
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:41,417
Aren't the national qualifiers tomorrow?

40
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:54,542
Come on, please don't say that.

41
00:04:54,667 --> 00:04:56,208
That's not what I mean!

42
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,958
I'm telling you to go give it to him.

43
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,583
To that guy.

44
00:05:11,042 --> 00:05:12,667
Don't end up like me.

45
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:17,333
It's better to regret doing something

46
00:05:19,792 --> 00:05:23,583
than to regret never trying at all.

47
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:35,208
Anyway, about what happened before...

48
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:38,250
I wanted to apologize.

49
00:05:38,375 --> 00:05:42,375
I hear two guys dating never lasts anyway.
Don't take it too seriously.

50
00:05:58,125 --> 00:05:59,885
[National High School
Basketball Tournament]

51
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,083
Nice! Keep the pressure on!

52
00:06:06,875 --> 00:06:08,125
Go for it!

53
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,625
Yes!

54
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,708
Nice shot!

55
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:24,667
Way to go! That's it!

56
00:06:25,792 --> 00:06:27,958
He's amazing. Harutora is so incredible!

57
00:06:31,458 --> 00:06:33,750
Isn't number eight from Sofu super hot?

58
00:06:33,875 --> 00:06:34,875
Sofu?

59
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,833
Turns out his name is Kurobe Harutora.

60
00:06:36,958 --> 00:06:38,208
Wait...

61
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:39,667
Isn't that him over there?

62
00:06:40,083 --> 00:06:42,417
- Did you see that?
- He's so gorgeous!

63
00:06:42,542 --> 00:06:43,875
Senpai.

64
00:06:45,417 --> 00:06:46,625
Harutora.

65
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,125
I'm so glad.

66
00:06:53,792 --> 00:06:56,083
I was afraid you wouldn't come.

67
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:59,500
Um...

68
00:06:59,958 --> 00:07:01,833
- Harutora...
- And about the lemons...

69
00:07:01,958 --> 00:07:03,542
Thank you, senpai.

70
00:07:04,708 --> 00:07:06,917
Thanks to them, I was full of energy.

71
00:07:10,417 --> 00:07:12,167
I'm sorry.

72
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:16,375
I wasn't there for you
when it mattered most.

73
00:07:17,917 --> 00:07:19,292
It's okay.

74
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,958
I understand how you felt.

75
00:07:27,417 --> 00:07:31,167
Oh, I saved a seat for you over there!

76
00:07:31,292 --> 00:07:32,500
Huh?

77
00:07:33,042 --> 00:07:33,667
[Reserved Seating]

78
00:07:33,792 --> 00:07:35,333
Ah!

79
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:42,708
Harutora, let's move!

80
00:07:44,792 --> 00:07:47,625
Keep cheering for me, okay?

81
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,000
Yeah.

82
00:07:50,417 --> 00:07:51,583
Harutora!

83
00:08:13,042 --> 00:08:17,042
Actually... I came out to my mom.

84
00:08:17,167 --> 00:08:18,792
I told her that I'm gay.

85
00:08:22,125 --> 00:08:25,167
I'm sorry I took it out
on you the other day.

86
00:08:26,958 --> 00:08:28,250
It's fine.

87
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:30,667
I panicked,

88
00:08:32,375 --> 00:08:33,792
and I was hurting.

89
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:39,625
I never even considered...

90
00:08:41,875 --> 00:08:46,333
how my mom must have felt on her way home.

91
00:08:53,625 --> 00:08:55,208
So...

92
00:08:56,667 --> 00:09:00,625
I want to have a proper talk with her.

93
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:05,917
I want to apologize for
giving her such a shock.

94
00:09:07,958 --> 00:09:13,167
Still... I also want her to know

95
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:19,292
that I have someone
really important to me now.

96
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,792
You're not forcing yourself, are you?

97
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,833
I'm not forcing anything...

98
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:31,958
Still...

99
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:38,500
Couldn't she have shown
a little understanding?

100
00:09:39,417 --> 00:09:45,292
Even just saying, "That took a lot of
courage," or "You must have had it rough."

101
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:52,083
She's my mom, after all.

102
00:10:00,792 --> 00:10:02,042
It's all right.

103
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:10,625
Ever since I met you, senpai,
everything began for me.

104
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:17,458
My life only truly started
after I met you.

105
00:10:20,833 --> 00:10:22,458
So, don't worry.

106
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,542
Here.

107
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,083
Um, Mom, there's something I want to say...

108
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:51,542
Oh, Sui!

109
00:10:52,042 --> 00:10:55,792
Your dad's transferring to Osaka
for work. He'll be living alone there.

110
00:10:56,083 --> 00:10:57,208
Huh?

111
00:10:57,333 --> 00:11:00,333
Right, I mentioned that last time.

112
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,417
Ah, I need to drop off a flyer next door.

113
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:07,875
Mom!

114
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:12,042
Uh...

115
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:13,375
Um...

116
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:16,167
I'm going to run to the store.

117
00:11:17,167 --> 00:11:18,417
Okay.

118
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,583
Mom.

119
00:11:22,917 --> 00:11:25,250
I have a K-drama to catch up on.

120
00:11:26,292 --> 00:11:27,625
I see.

121
00:11:43,525 --> 00:11:44,845
[Conversation with Harutora]

122
00:11:45,131 --> 00:11:47,458
"That's Suzuki."

123
00:11:48,542 --> 00:11:49,917
Suzuki?

124
00:11:53,042 --> 00:11:54,958
[Apple Pie]

125
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:58,625
Daiki?

126
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:03,515
[I love you, senpai] [I love you, senpai]
[Hidden Acrostic Message]

127
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:07,542
"I love Sui senpai the most."

128
00:12:10,292 --> 00:12:13,333
Honestly, Harutora is such a goof.

129
00:12:16,083 --> 00:12:17,375
I'm home.

130
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:18,833
Welcome back, Mom.

131
00:12:18,958 --> 00:12:20,958
Um, there's something I
want to talk to you about.

132
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,750
How did you know?

133
00:12:31,875 --> 00:12:33,792
That I had a fever?

134
00:12:38,792 --> 00:12:41,833
I guess I learned a lot
from living in the dorms.

135
00:12:42,708 --> 00:12:43,958
Really?

136
00:12:44,875 --> 00:12:46,542
Well, it's just...

137
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:51,750
cooking and cleaning for myself,

138
00:12:52,250 --> 00:12:54,250
and talking to all kinds of people.

139
00:12:55,792 --> 00:13:02,917
Over time, I started paying more
attention to what's around me.

140
00:13:06,375 --> 00:13:08,875
Still, I can't do what you do, Mom.

141
00:13:09,833 --> 00:13:12,208
Just from hearing someone's voice,

142
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:16,583
you instantly know if
they aren't feeling well.

143
00:13:22,667 --> 00:13:27,375
Ever since that day, I've
looked up a lot on my own.

144
00:13:38,708 --> 00:13:41,750
Logically, I understand it,

145
00:13:43,083 --> 00:13:47,833
but it might take me a
little time to truly accept it.

146
00:13:55,792 --> 00:13:59,250
Even so, Sui...

147
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:04,875
I just want you to be happy.

148
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:11,208
You know...

149
00:14:11,542 --> 00:14:15,792
getting pregnant with
you was truly a miracle.

150
00:14:17,792 --> 00:14:22,625
I wanted to give up so many
times, but I couldn't let go.

151
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:27,292
After going through so much despair,

152
00:14:27,417 --> 00:14:30,042
we were finally blessed with you.

153
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:36,000
From the day you were born,

154
00:14:37,583 --> 00:14:41,458
you brought us nothing but pure joy.

155
00:14:43,375 --> 00:14:45,000
So, Sui...

156
00:14:47,042 --> 00:14:48,542
Promise me,

157
00:14:50,667 --> 00:14:54,542
you have to live a happy life.

158
00:14:56,250 --> 00:15:01,250
No matter which path you
take, you must be happy.

159
00:15:01,375 --> 00:15:03,750
You have to promise me that, all right?

160
00:15:12,708 --> 00:15:14,042
I will.

161
00:15:18,458 --> 00:15:19,792
Mom...

162
00:15:23,208 --> 00:15:27,208
I promise.

163
00:15:33,208 --> 00:15:39,500
Um... there's someone
really important to me now.

164
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:44,958
You mean you're seeing someone?

165
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:46,667
Yeah.

166
00:15:48,292 --> 00:15:49,167
Oh?

167
00:15:49,292 --> 00:15:50,708
Who is it?

168
00:15:54,292 --> 00:15:55,875
It's him.

169
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,083
I knew it was him.

170
00:16:03,417 --> 00:16:05,000
How did you know?

171
00:16:05,625 --> 00:16:09,083
I am your mother, after all.

172
00:16:09,750 --> 00:16:11,375
Ah.

173
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:15,250
Of course you are.

174
00:16:15,375 --> 00:16:17,417
I see.

175
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,208
Senpai, it's me!

176
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:43,083
What's wrong, Harutora?

177
00:16:43,208 --> 00:16:44,518
While I was waiting for
you outside the dorm,

178
00:16:44,542 --> 00:16:47,542
everyone kept asking me what I was doing.

179
00:16:47,667 --> 00:16:50,083
Have you been waiting
for me this whole time?

180
00:16:50,667 --> 00:16:52,208
Because I couldn't stop worrying...

181
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:54,667
I wanted to know how
things went with your family.

182
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:56,958
Ah...

183
00:17:07,625 --> 00:17:09,458
It looks like it didn't go so well...

184
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:11,833
Huh?

185
00:17:12,833 --> 00:17:14,958
You don't have to force a smile, senpai.

186
00:17:15,083 --> 00:17:16,125
I...

187
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:18,370
You can take your anger
out on me. Really, it's fine.

188
00:17:18,708 --> 00:17:20,167
Wait...

189
00:17:20,667 --> 00:17:21,958
No, that's not it!

190
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:26,958
The talk with my mom
actually went pretty well.

191
00:17:27,875 --> 00:17:31,625
I just wanted to take my
time and tell you properly later.

192
00:17:32,708 --> 00:17:35,917
I still haven't told my dad, though,

193
00:17:36,042 --> 00:17:38,625
so it's not like everything
is completely resolved.

194
00:17:39,417 --> 00:17:44,625
Still, my mom wants me to be happy.

195
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,042
Really?

196
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:50,042
Yeah.

197
00:17:51,375 --> 00:17:57,333
She even put on the heels
I bought for her back then.

198
00:17:58,167 --> 00:18:01,167
The ones she wore to the
parent-teacher conference?

199
00:18:01,292 --> 00:18:03,792
Yeah. You remember that?

200
00:18:12,667 --> 00:18:14,167
And you know what?

201
00:18:16,292 --> 00:18:19,917
I told her everything.

202
00:18:20,042 --> 00:18:22,375
I told her that I'm dating someone.

203
00:18:23,875 --> 00:18:27,625
When she found out it
was you, she was thrilled.

204
00:18:29,958 --> 00:18:31,667
Really?

205
00:18:31,792 --> 00:18:33,042
Yeah.

206
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:40,042
Thank goodness...

207
00:18:41,458 --> 00:18:43,417
I'm so relieved...

208
00:18:48,208 --> 00:18:49,708
Thank you.

209
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:52,250
It's all thanks to you, Harutora.

210
00:18:54,208 --> 00:18:55,958
No, it's not.

211
00:18:56,083 --> 00:18:58,208
It's all because of your
own courage, senpai.

212
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:35,059
All right, Kishida-kun, your turn.

213
00:19:35,083 --> 00:19:36,208
Okay.

214
00:19:45,542 --> 00:19:47,292
I'm Kurobe Harutora,

215
00:19:47,417 --> 00:19:48,875
second-year.

216
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,208
Sui senpai...

217
00:19:50,917 --> 00:19:53,875
I'm currently dating Sui senpai.

218
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:59,708
I love the honeyed lemons he makes for me.

219
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,208
Come on, spill it!

220
00:20:12,333 --> 00:20:13,208
We're friends, aren't we?

221
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:14,792
Aren't we friends?

222
00:20:14,917 --> 00:20:16,250
- Senpai.
- Yeah?

223
00:20:16,708 --> 00:20:18,125
I really don't think...

224
00:20:18,250 --> 00:20:19,810
you should be doing that kind of thing.

225
00:20:20,833 --> 00:20:22,250
It's fine!

226
00:20:22,375 --> 00:20:22,958
I was just joking!

227
00:20:23,083 --> 00:20:25,123
- Don't take it so seriously.
- Just kidding around!

228
00:20:46,250 --> 00:20:49,708
[Sofu High School Graduation Ceremony]

229
00:20:50,417 --> 00:20:52,792
[Aoba Student Dormitory]

230
00:20:56,250 --> 00:20:57,833
Senpai.

231
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:01,833
Congratulations on graduating.

232
00:21:03,375 --> 00:21:04,375
Thank you.

233
00:21:06,917 --> 00:21:08,958
How were these three years?

234
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,167
Well...

235
00:21:17,708 --> 00:21:19,125
I'm really gonna miss it.

236
00:21:20,708 --> 00:21:22,083
Huh?

237
00:21:24,708 --> 00:21:26,417
I'm really gonna miss this place.

238
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:34,958
I'm glad to hear that.

239
00:21:42,458 --> 00:21:43,792
Harutora.

240
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:51,083
I...

241
00:21:57,458 --> 00:21:59,708
I'm so glad I can finally be myself.

242
00:22:04,875 --> 00:22:06,542
I'm truly happy.

243
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,417
Senpai...

244
00:22:17,417 --> 00:22:18,958
Isn't that...

245
00:22:19,292 --> 00:22:20,917
just the way it should be?

246
00:23:42,833 --> 00:23:44,875
[This program is a work of fiction.]
